**Benefits of Movement to Work**

Taking part can help participants:

* Gain practical workplace experience
* Build confidence in a professional environment
* Develop transferable skills
* Improve communication skills
* Develop teamwork skills
* Improve time-management skills
* Build technical and digital skills
* Improve their CV
* Prepare for interviews
* Gain experience they can discuss during future applications
* Better understand different job roles and industries
* Receive evidence of participation that can strengthen their CV
* Move closer towards employment or further training

**Skelmersdale Jobcentre Programme Overview**

The Skelmersdale Jobcentre Movement to Work programme is a two-week work-experience programme.
Participants will attend for approximately **six days across the two weeks**, running from **Monday to Wednesday**, with sessions taking place at approximately **10:00am–3:00pm**.
The programme is designed to give participants practical experience while helping them become more confident and better prepared for employment.

**The programme aims to:

* Introduce participants to different roles within the Jobcentre
* Provide practical workplace experience
* Help participants recognise existing transferable skills
* Help participants develop new transferable skills
* Build workplace confidence
* Improve communication and social skills
* Develop teamwork and time-management skills
* Improve technical and digital skills
* Support participants with creating or improving their CV
* Explain how CVs can be tailored towards specific roles
* Provide support with cover letters
* Provide support with personal statements
* Improve job-application skills
* Provide interview preparation and mock interview experience
* Explain how AI can be used appropriately when preparing applications
* Give participants experience they can add to their CV
* Help participants become more work-ready
* Encourage more eligible Jobcentre customers to take part in the programme

The website should clearly communicate what participants will do, what they will gain and how the two-week programme can help them prepare for future employment.
